From a1336027a70b0dc910bdde52a6fa245d712605ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charles Hoskinson <charles.hoskinson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:29:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] T7: root statement and seal of L, bound iface run,
 t7_chain example

- stmt: the L root statement takes the key constants (SEG, h_lo, keys_d, N3 pre-hash) as
  constants and sends (prog_d, post_d) to RootSealAir, which opens post_d (X10), checks the
  seal predicates and exposes the three R operand digests (frozen L budgets: 2,000 columns,
  100 interactions per AIR).
- Node and Fv share one AIR shape; merge refusals produce a forced output for mutant cases.
- iface: case_run_bound (root_stmt and the R run operands from L), reservation_full.
- lverify: gen_r_check returns mode and open; gen_ops_check also checks A_0 = C_P.
- t7_chain: chain (leaf, N1, N2, N3, L, L_Fr, L refusals) and cases (N1 refusals, mixed chip
  sets, the FV unit under N3).
